stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> ONLINE: Admin: POST /gates\n(registered, auto-pinged)

    ONLINE --> OFFLINE: Ping fails\n(ConnectException or non-2xx HTTP response)\nGatePing background job detects failure

    OFFLINE --> ONLINE: Ping succeeds\n(next scheduled ping cycle)

    ONLINE --> DISABLED: Admin: POST /gates (update with status=DISABLED)\n(manual disable, e.g. maintenance)

    OFFLINE --> DISABLED: Admin manually disables\nunreachable gate

    DISABLED --> ONLINE: Admin re-enables gate\nAND next ping succeeds

    ONLINE --> Deleted: Admin: DELETE /gates/{gateId}

    OFFLINE --> Deleted: Admin: DELETE /gates/{gateId}

    DISABLED --> Deleted: Admin: DELETE /gates/{gateId}

    Deleted --> [*]: Gate removed from registry\nNo longer used in broadcasts

    note right of ONLINE
        Status: ONLINE
        - Included in identifier search broadcasts
        - gateRegistry.online() returns this gate
        - Last successful ping recorded
        - eDelivery or Fast HTTP calls routed here
    end note

    note right of OFFLINE
        Status: OFFLINE
        - Excluded from identifier search broadcasts
        - gateRegistry.online() does NOT return this gate
        - Direct dataset requests (GET /dataset/{eu-fi01}/...) fail
          with 502 Bad Gateway
        - Ping job continues trying to reconnect
    end note

    note right of DISABLED
        Status: DISABLED
        - Excluded from broadcasts AND ping job
        - gateRegistry.enabled() does NOT return this gate
        - Admin explicitly disabled (e.g. scheduled maintenance)
        - Will NOT auto-recover (requires admin re-enable)
    end note
